# The Perseus Project and Beyond: How Building a Digital Library Challenges the Humanities and Technology.

**Authors:** Crane, Gregory

## Abstract
The Perseus Project, a digital library in the humanities concentrating on ancient Greek culture, is expanding to cover Roman, Renaissance and various other areas of the humanities. Goals include helping traditional scholars research effectively and help humanists use technology to redefine the relationship between their work and the broader intellectual community. (Author/JMK)

